[AUDIT vs the repository Theorem 8]
  Theorem 8 (paper, \label{thm:zetasharp}) defines  Q_rest(f) = Q_0(f) - 4F(gamma)^2
  where Q_0 is the AUGMENTED COUNTERFACTUAL baseline of notes/proofs.md section B.1,
  convention 3: a DOUBLE on-line pair at gamma that is then moved off the line.
  Its baseline therefore contains 4F(gamma)^2 = the collapsed quartet, and its
  "remaining" form is what is left after removing those FOUR zeros.

  Our Q_rest removes the FOUR ACTUAL zeros of the orbit O_1, at their actual
  displacement delta_1, not a collapsed double pair.  The two agree in the
  multiplicity convention (four zeros removed, four zeros in the orbit) and differ
  in that ours is evaluated at delta_1 > 0 while Theorem 8 removes the delta = 0
  limit.  The difference is exactly Q_{O_1}(delta_1) - Q_{O_1}(0), which Phase G
  measures.

  Theorem 8 ASSUMES "every nontrivial zero other than the one being moved lies on
  the critical line", and states this as SUFFICIENT for Q_rest >= 0.  For the
  Davenport-Heilbronn function that hypothesis is FALSE: the census finds further
  off-line quartets.  So Theorem 8 does not apply here, and we do NOT assume it.

  Does its PROOF transfer under the weaker hypothesis "Q_rest >= 0"?  Yes, and
  trivially: the proof uses the hypothesis ONLY through the single inequality
  Qtilde >= 0 (notes/proofs.md, Theorem B' proof: "Q_delta >= 0 + 0 - 4 delta^2 F'^2
  - delta^4 F''^2 - |R_4|").  Nothing else about the location of the other zeros is
  used.  Therefore the conclusion
      lambda_min(Q_delta) >= -4 K(L,gamma) delta^2 - (2/5 + (16/3) e^{2 L delta}) L^5 delta^4
  holds verbatim with "all other zeros on the line" replaced by "Q_rest >= 0 on the
  admissible sector".  That is a strictly weaker hypothesis, and it is the one this
  phase measures.  What does NOT transfer is any claim that the measured positivity
  of a finite Galerkin restriction establishes that hypothesis (see below).

  CAUTION.  A positive finite restriction of Q_rest does NOT establish the
  whole-window Theorem 8 hypothesis.  Classification R6 is not reported anywhere in
  this extension.

